  "description": "X2 Enduro — the finest X2 yet\nThe X2 is Luna's improved successor to the popular X1 — a carbon full-suspension enduro eMTB with RockShox and SRAM spec that outperforms OEM rivals costing twice as much, and stays stealthy enough to pass as a regular tricked-out enduro bike. Class 2 pedelec.\n\nBafang M600 mid drive — 750W, over 95Nm torque, torque sensor (5 levels) + throttle\n48V 17.5Ah LG battery (820Wh) — 20% larger than the X1, removable, locking\nSilent carbon PEEK gear standard (normally $300)\nRockShox suspension — 160mm Yari fork, Deluxe Select+ shock\nSRAM 12-speed & 4-piston brakes; 27.5\" or 29er wheel options\n\nSpecifications\n\nMotor\nBafang M600 mid drive, 750W, >95Nm, torque sensor (5 levels) + throttle, 7 lb, 36:1 reduction\n\nBattery\n48V 17.5Ah LG cells, 820Wh (20% larger than X1), removable downtube, 2 keys, power switch, charge port\n\nBrakes\nSRAM Guide 4-piston hydraulic, 200mm front / 180mm rear\n\nWheels\n27.5\" (2.8\" tires, 39mm rims) or 29er (2.6\" tires, 34mm rims); Maxxis or WTB, double-wall 40mm\n\nFrame\nCarbon fiber; dropper post, internal cables, Boost thru-axles\n\nSizes\nS 16\" / M 17.5\" / L 19\" / XL 21\"\n\nWarranty\n2yr carbon frame, 1yr battery, 1yr PEEK gear, 6mo motor/components\n\nA legit enduro eMTB\nTop-end components on a carbon frame, with a torque-sensing M600 that feels like a natural extension of your legs and is Class-1 trail legal in non-Ludicrous mode. Add the optional Ludicrous V2 controller for up to 60 battery amps in bursts, 50%+ more torque, and a Bluetooth app — note that the Ludicrous upgrade makes the bike no longer road legal in many USA states.\n29er or 27.5?\nBoth wheel options are available. The 29er rolls faster over obstacles and holds speed; the 27.5 is more playful and accelerates quicker. Choose based on your terrain and riding style.\n\nThe Ludicrous upgrade makes the bike no longer road legal in many USA states. The buyer takes full responsibility for proper use of this product.",
